        "original_id": "fbc7c579-5271-5036-a7bb-b969e9356b25",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bruce Dayton, George Draper Dayton\n- Companies: The Dayton Company, Dayton's department store, Dayton Hudson Corporation, Target Corporation\n- Roles: Chief executive officer, chairman, founder\n\nFacts:\n- George Draper Dayton was an American businessman and philanthropist who founded Dayton's department store, which later became Target Corporation.\n- Bruce Dayton was one of the five Dayton brothers, all grandsons of George Draper Dayton, founder of The Dayton Company.\n- The five Dayton brothers expanded their grandfather's Dayton's department store in downtown Minneapolis from a single location into the national Target Corporation, one of the largest retail chains in the United States.\n- Bruce Dayton was the last surviving member of the five Dayton brothers.\n- Bruce Dayton served as chief executive officer of Dayton Hudson Corporation, the company now known as Target Corporation.\n- Bruce Dayton became chairman of Dayton Hudson Corporation and served in that role from 1970 to 1977.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2eb61f11-62fc-549d-bb78-6cc4de57531d",
        "text": "Page: Bruce Dayton. Sentence: Dayton was the last surviving of member of the five Dayton brothers – all grandsons of George Dayton, the founder of The Dayton Company – who expanded their grandfather's Dayton's department store in downtown Minneapolis from a single location into the national Target Corporation, one of the largest retail store chains in the United States.\nPage: Bruce Dayton. Sentence: Dayton served as the chief executive officer (CEO) of the Dayton Hudson Corporation, the company now known as the Target Corporation, before becoming the chairman of Dayton Hudson from 1970 to 1977.\nPage: George Dayton. Sentence: George Draper Dayton (March 6, 1857 – February 18, 1938) was an American businessman and philanthropist, most famous for being the founder of Dayton's department store, which later became Target Corporation.",
